# Uber patient sex + portrait integrity (learn-from-mistakes)

A patient's sex is derived from **three independent sources**. They drive different
things and they can silently disagree — that is exactly how Ruth Okonkwo (U15) shipped
as a *woman in the portrait but a man in the attending/patient voice*.

## The three sources (and what each one drives)

| Source | Field | Drives |
|---|---|---|
| `src/data/patientUberRefs.json` → `refs[slug].sex` | face-slug sex | **Portrait + game-scene** template (`resolvePortraitSex` checks this FIRST) |
| `src/data/uberCases.json` → `patientSex` | case-level | Case context / documentation source of truth |
| `src/data/preparedCases.json` → `cases[id].patientSex` | prepared | **Patient-sim voice + pronouns** via `resolvePatientSex` |

**Precedence trap:** `preparedCases` defaults `patientSex` to `"male"` for almost every
case (template leak). So a female-named patient with a female face slug will still be
*voiced male* unless `preparedCases.cases[id].patientSex` is explicitly `"female"`.
The portrait looks right; the sim is wrong. Always set **all three** to the same value.

## Non-negotiable rule

Whenever you touch an Uber case's sex, name, `faceSlug`, portrait, or the patient sim:

1. The patient's name/identity, the face-slug sex, `uberCases.patientSex`, and
   `preparedCases.cases[id].patientSex` must **all agree**.
2. A male patient must not carry a female face slug (or vice-versa) — that is the
   same bug seen from the portrait side (U11 Darius Webb was on `copper-afro-headwrap-africa`).
3. **Run the audit and reach `0 problem case(s)` before serving / committing:**

   ```bash
   node scripts/audit-uber-sex.mjs
   ```

   It cross-checks all three sources for every Uber case and flags `MISMATCH` / `NO-SEX`.
   `scripts/fix-uber-sex.mjs` is the corrective pass it was written alongside.

## How to fix a mismatch

- Wrong sim voice (female patient sounds male): set
  `preparedCases.cases[id].patientSex = "female"` **and** `uberCases.patientSex = "female"`.
- Wrong portrait (male patient, female face): repoint `uberCases.faceSlug` and
  `patientUberRefs.caseSlugs[id]` to a slug whose `refs[slug].sex` matches, and keep
  the `refs[].uberCases` lists honest.
- Pediatric patients use `pediatricFaceSlug` (not in `refs`), so `portraitSex` can't read
  their sex from a slug — `patientSex` in both case files is the only guard. Set it.

## Meta (why this rule exists)

This rule was written *after* the agent shipped a sex mismatch the user had to catch.
The lesson generalizes: when a single fact (sex, name, vitals, diagnosis) lives in more
than one data file, do not patch one file and assume the rest follow. Find every source,
write/keep an audit script, and run it to green before declaring done. Add a similar
audit + rule the next time a multi-source field bites — don't wait to be told.
